course: dictionary
lesson: 10188
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and time is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» Here time means how long something lasts, not the clock on the wall.
explain: Look at the words next to time. «What time is it?» asks for the hour on a clock. «The first time» means one occasion. «3 times 4 is 12» uses times to mean multiplied by. Ask which meaning fits, then try it in the sentence.
explain: Some phrases use time in a special way, so learn them as a whole. «On time» means not late, and «in time» means early enough. «Time's up» means the time has finished. When context does not settle it, check a dictionary.
fact: Time can be a noun or a verb: you can have time, or you can time a race.
fact: «Time» means how long something lasts, measured in seconds, minutes, hours, days and years.
fact: «Times» means multiplied by, so 3 times 4 is 12.
fact: «Time out» is a short break, and «about time!» means at last, when you are late.
fact: «On time» can mean different things in different places, so check the context.
exercise: «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» In this sentence, what does time mean? | The hour shown on a clock | *How long something lasts | A period in history | One occasion when something happens
exercise: «3 times 4 is 12.» What does times mean here? | Occasions | Periods of history | Hours | *Multiplied by
exercise: Maya says «Time the race with a stopwatch.» What does time mean here? | To make a clock | A short break | To be late | *To measure how long something takes
test: «What time is it?» asks for what? | One occasion when something happens | The times tables | The length of a film | *The hour and minutes shown on a clock
test: Ben got to the bus stop with a minute to spare, so he was in time. What does «in time» mean? | Very angry | Running fast | Lost | *Early enough
exam: Read «the same sloth can swim across a river about three times faster than it climbs». What does three times faster mean? | *About three times as fast | Faster than a clock | Three hours faster | Very slowly
